Z||000002||TheFiero64||11-08-2000||01:32 PM||||I just remembered by looking at it that the 88 block is different. It has none on the intake side. Here is a pic of the 88 block. I notice there are 2 in the back of the block under where the bell housing would be. Here are some pics I just snapped. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/block3.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/block4.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/block1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/block2.jpg"> <BR>I know its not what you needed but I ope it may help someone.<P>------------------<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||11-08-2000||07:21 PM||||Trivia maybe..... the big hole in the second picture next to the timing gear is for the water pump when this block is used in an S10 pickup. It's not a freeze plug of any type. In 87-88 Fiero the hole is covered by the Serpent tensioner but in most other cars it's got a simple steel cover.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 11-08-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Gold-86SE||11-08-2000||07:47 PM||||<BR>Guys, thanks for the help.  That block looks to be the same as mine.  Thanks again.<BR>||||reg||1
